    "question": {
      ":question/id": "9721adeb-922f-509c-976c-2314e429797a",
      ":question/problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & 6 & -11 \\\\ -6 & -4 & 2 & -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & 6 & -11 \\\\ -6 & -4 & 2 & -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{3} :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & -4 & 2 & -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{4} :={R}_{4}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $4$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $4.$",
